    "description": "Pine Gate Renewables is a developer and owner-operator of utility-scale solar and storage projects in the United States. Its customers are utilities, corporate offtakers, and grid markets that require large-scale renewable generation and storage capacity. The model combines project development and long-term asset ownership, making it both capital-intensive and reliant on recurring infrastructure deployment. Company materials state that Pine Gate was founded in 2016 and operates across the United States, while Generate announced a US$500 million strategic growth and asset-financing commitment in 2022. The reviewed materials did not disclose Generate's ownership percentage in the platform. Generate remained an investor in 2024 when Pine Gate announced the final closing of a US$650 million investment that also included HOOPP and HESTA.",
